{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YNfCvzsJkcmk93utH24jSu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `picoquic/picosocks.h` plus the Phase 2 socket\n2\t//! abstraction.\n3\t//!\n4\t//! Phase 2 reshape: the C `SOCKET_TYPE` (a Linux file descriptor)\n5\t//! is replaced by a [`Socket`] *trait* that the host platform\n6\t//! implements.  The default implementation wraps\n7\t//! [`socket2::Socket`] (the canonical cross-platform UDP socket\n8\t//! crate); other backends (no-std embedded, Windows-specific,\n9\t//! the test simulator) implement the same trait.\n10\t//! [`ServerSockets<S>`] is generic over the implementor.\n11\t//!\n12\t//! Phase 1 contract: signatures only — every method body is\n13\t//! `todo!()`.\n14\t\n15\tuse core::net::SocketAddr;\n16\t\n17\tuse crate::Error;\n18\tuse crate::Instant;\n19\t\n20\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n21\t// Constants and supporting types.\n22\t\n23\t/// Number of UDP sockets a server context owns — one IPv4, one\n24\t/// IPv6.  C: `PICOQUIC_NB_SERVER_SOCKETS`.\n25\tpub const SERVER_SOCKET_COUNT: usize = 2;\n26\t\n27\t/// `MessageHeader` is a re-export of [`socket2::MsgHdr`] — the\n28\t/// canonical cross-platform `msghdr` wrapper.  Phase 4 fills in\n29\t/// the bodies that thread one through the cmsg helpers.\n30\tpub type MessageHeader<'addr, 'bufs, 'control> = socket2::MsgHdr<'addr, 'bufs, 'control>;\n31\t\n32\t/// OS error code surfaced by socket sends when the underlying\n33\t/// syscall fails.  Wraps the raw Linux `errno` (or its Windows\n34\t/// equivalent on other targets) and exposes\n35\t/// [`OsError::is_unreachable`] for the path-abandon decision the\n36\t/// C `picoquic_socket_error_implies_unreachable` helper made.\n37\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n38\tpub struct OsError(pub i32);\n39\t\n40\timpl OsError {\n41\t    /// Whether this errno implies the destination is unreachable\n42\t    /// and the owning path should be abandoned.  C:\n43\t    /// `picoquic_socket_error_implies_unreachable`.\n44\t    pub fn is_unreachable(self) -> bool {\n45\t        todo!()\n46\t    }\n47\t}\n48\t\n49\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n50\t// `Socket` trait.\n51\t\n52\t/// One UDP socket on the application's network stack.  Replaces\n53\t/// the C `SOCKET_TYPE` (a raw file descriptor); the host\n54\t/// implementation supplies open / bind / send / recv operations\n55\t/// while the rest of picoquic stays platform-agnostic.\n56\t///\n57\t/// The default [`socket2::Socket`] implementation is in\n58\t/// [`crate::socks_socket2`] (gated on the `std` feature).\n59\tpub trait Socket {\n60\t    /// Local address bound to this socket (`getsockname`).\n61\t    /// C: `picoquic_get_local_address`.\n62\t    fn local_address(&self) -> Result<SocketAddr, Error>;\n63\t\n64\t    /// Receive one UDP datagram into `buffer`.  Output parameters\n65\t    /// (source / dest address, interface index, ECN, byte count)\n66\t    /// fold into [`RecvInfo`]; the slice length subsumes the C\n67\t    /// `buffer_max` parameter.  C: `picoquic_recvmsg`.\n68\t    fn recv(&mut self, buffer: &mut [u8]) -> Result<RecvInfo, Error>;\n69\t\n70\t    /// Send `bytes` to `addr_dest` from `addr_from` with an\n71\t    /// optional GSO segmentation hint `gso_size` (`UDP_SEGMENT`).\n72\t    /// `addr_from = None` lets the kernel choose the source\n73\t    /// address.  `Ok(n)` reports bytes sent; `Err` carries the\n74\t    /// OS error.  C: `picoquic_sendmsg`.\n75\t    fn send(\n76\t        &mut self,\n77\t        addr_dest: &SocketAddr,\n78\t        addr_from: Option<&SocketAddr>,\n79\t        dest_if: i32,\n80\t        bytes: &[u8],\n81\t        gso_size: i32,\n82\t    ) -> Result<usize, OsError>;\n83\t\n84\t    /// Enable per-packet destination-info delivery on this\n85\t    /// socket (`IP_PKTINFO` / `IPV6_RECVPKTINFO`).  Default:\n86\t    /// no-op for backends that don't